              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every trailer driver knows that safety doesn't begin when you hit the highway; it starts before you even pull out of the lot. Whether you're hauling freight across the state or preparing for a long-distance run, inspecting each critical <a href=\"/parts\">trailer part</a> can help prevent breakdowns, accidents, and costly delays.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While the temptation might be to do a quick walkaround and say that everything is fine, the reality is that trailer issues account for a large number of roadside violations and service calls. The good news? Most of these problems can be avoided with a thorough inspection and a solid understanding of which parts need your attention. Here's a breakdown of the most important trailer components to check before every trip.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
