                          "props": {
                            "text": "Landing Gear",
                            "headingLevel": 2,
                            "align": "left",
                            "anchor": "step-2"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "p-step-2",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Don't overlook your landing gear, especially if you're dropping and hooking often. These legs support the front of your trailer when it's detached, and damaged or poorly functioning landing gear can make for a tough time at the yard. Check for signs of damage to the legs, crank, and gearbox. Make sure the landing gear raises and lowers smoothly, and that all bolts are tight and secure. A simple failure here can turn into a serious downtime issue if you're not careful.",
                            "align": "left",
                            "width": "full"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
