                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "p-step-3",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Every seasoned hauler knows that tire issues are one of the most common, and avoidable, problems on the road. Look for proper inflation, tread wear, and visible damage like cuts, bulges, or foreign objects. Don't forget to inspect the inner sidewalls and valve stems. Also, make sure your wheels and lug nuts are in good shape. Cracked or bent rims can weaken under stress, and loose lug nuts can cause serious damage or even wheel detachment.",
                            "align": "left",
                            "width": "full"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
