                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "p-step-4",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Faulty lighting is one of the top reasons for roadside stops. Before hitting the road, test your brake lights, turn signals, tail lights, and clearance lights. Make sure your electrical pigtail is securely connected and there's no damage to the wires or plug. You should also check the wiring along the trailer body for wear or exposed connections. Any broken or dim light isn't just unsafe; it's a violation waiting to happen.",
                            "align": "left",
                            "width": "full"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
