                        },
                        {
                          "id": "p-step-5",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Trailer brakes do a lot of the heavy lifting when it comes to stopping power, especially under load. Make sure the air lines are secure and not rubbing or leaking. Check your brakes and brake pads for visible wear or damage. Listen for air leaks during your pre-trip check and verify that your air pressure builds and holds properly. A faulty brake component isn't something you want to discover on a steep downhill grade.",
                            "align": "left",
